---
import AppDocLayout from '../../layouts/AppDocLayout.astro';
---

<AppDocLayout
  title="Fast Easy - Support"
  description="Get help with Fast Easy - Fasting Timer iOS app."
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/fast-easy/support"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-8">Support</h1>

        <div class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-12">
          <p class="text-lg mb-4">Need help with Fast Easy?</p>
          <p>Send us an email at <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Fast%20Easy%20Support%20Request" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a> and we'll get back to you as soon as we can.</p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="space-y-8 text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I start a fast?</h3>
            <p>Pick a plan, like 16:8, and tap Start fast. The timer keeps counting even when Fast Easy is closed. Tap End fast when you eat, or keep going past your goal.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">I started or ended a fast at the wrong time. Can I fix it?</h3>
            <p>Yes. While a fast is running, tap Started on the Timer to change when it began. For a past fast, open the menu, choose History, tap the fast, and change when it started or ended.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I add widgets?</h3>
            <p>Long-press your Home Screen, tap Edit, then Add Widget, search for “Fast Easy” and pick a size. For the Lock Screen, long-press it, tap Customize, then Lock Screen, and add Fast Easy. Widgets show time to go and fill their flag when you reach your goal.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Why don’t I see the Live Activity?</h3>
            <p>It starts when you start a fast on iPhone. If it doesn’t appear, check that Live Activities are on in Settings → Fast Easy, then open Fast Easy while a fast is running.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I get a reminder when I reach my goal?</h3>
            <p>Open the menu, tap Settings, and turn on Goal reminder. Fast Easy sends one notification when your fast reaches its goal.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Where does the weight trend come from?</h3>
            <p>Apple Health. If you allow it, Fast Easy reads your body weight to show its trend in Statistics. It never writes to Apple Health. To change access, open the Health app, tap your profile, then Apps → Fast Easy.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I change the dial, colors or app icon?</h3>
            <p>Swipe the dial on the Timer to switch between Classic, Clock, Segments and Minimal. In Settings, choose Light or Dark (with Graphite or Black at night) and one of eight accents; each accent comes with its own app icon.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Where is my data stored?</h3>
            <p>On your device. Nothing is sent to the cloud or any server, and there’s no account. Your fasts are included in your iCloud or computer backup, so restoring a backup on a new device brings them with it.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</AppDocLayout>
